Z||000009||FieroHeather||10-07-2001||09:50 PM||||Well, another holiday has just passed.  And the secret is out of the bag.<P>I am now permitted to tell people about my dad.  Two weeks ago he was diagnosed with Terminal Cancer.<P>The doctors dont know for sure, and we wont know until Thursday the results of his biopsies.  <P>We werent telling our family until today.  We have had our big cry, and now Im both full and drained at the same time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000010||FieroMontreal||10-07-2001||09:54 PM||||OMG, Heather I'm so sorry.. I can't find the words to explain my sorrow.. I hope they do find a way to help your father .. I'm sorry I can not do more then pray for his sake. I will pray for your family and hope that everyone else on these forums will do the same.<BR>-Alex<p>[This message has been edited by FieroMontreal (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000011||gt boy||10-07-2001||11:59 PM||||Heather I am saddened to hear about your fathers condition and hope for the best for you, your father and your family.  This type of news can really put a damper on the holidays...but that is what they are for, spending time with the people you love.<P>Hang tough girl ...you dad needs you to be strong. <P>Ernie<p>[This message has been edited by gt boy (edited 10-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||grinthock||10-08-2001||10:31 AM||||Thanks for the ThanksGiving wishes.... Both those and your prayers helped me drive to and from the PA show safely.<P>As for Dad, well, I guess with everyone knowing I can say this.<P>I have been a supporter of FieroHeather since this fiasco began almost a year ago with other complications, in and out of the hospital.  It's all very difficult, it's been hard and getting harder, I have watched the situation deterriorate, and I am STILL standing here for you Heather as I always have, you know my numbers, and my emails.<P>Heather's father is a great man.  A young guy at heart too, this is hard for me as I have been very close to him.<P>I remember months back when he was hospitalized (and under the care of doctors who paralized him with drugs while he could recover) he had little visitors for some time because he was in a city over 90 MILES from their family home, I live only 20, I would go there almost daily to visit him, and just talk to him.  He was awake, but couldn't open his eyes, OR speak, or move.  But he COULD hear.   You can all imagine how crazy this would make you.<P>The only response during those tough times was a VERY slight squeeze from his hands.<P>My prayers are with you Heather.  I pray daily for his recovery, and comfort.||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroHeather||10-09-2001||12:19 AM||||Thankyou Justin for all of your support you have provided my family this past year, and for all of the support you have been to me throughout this whole mess.  It means a lot to know that Im not alone with knowing about my Dad.<P>Thankyou Ernie and Alex for your warm wishes, and thoughts sent my way.  This is an extremely rough time, and I appreciate the support from my online PFF family  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||JSocha||10-09-2001||01:56 AM||||From this PFF member, you're definately welcome Heather.<P>Best wishes to you and your family.  We're here for you and your family will be in our thoughts as well.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Voytek||10-09-2001||11:25 AM||||Thanks for the holiday wishes!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>About your dad - perhaps 'speedy recovery' is not a realistic wish for your dad.  Know this: life on earth is only a short stop before eternal life.  Your dad is a lucky man to have a family that will see him off to a much better place; many people depart in loneliness, without a comforting touch or even so much as a small prayer.<P>Suffering is a part of our humanity (Sep. 11, 2001).  I hope you will be comforted knowing that you're not alone in this and our prayers are with you.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cheever3000||10-09-2001||08:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHeather:<BR>I am now permitted to tell people about my dad.  Two weeks ago he was diagnosed with Terminal Cancer.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I just now saw this.  I'm sending big hugs for you & your family, and prayers for your dad and all of you.  May you be given strength from Above, in addition to support & encouragement from those of us in this family.<P><BR>I came into this topic looking for the history of the Canadian Thanksgiving.  What started it, and what does it mean to you now?<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||K2m4||10-11-2001||10:59 AM||||Keep your head up Heather. They said the same thing about my mom seven years ago. She was Diagnosed with terminal cancer of the lymph nodes  and in her thyroid and was given less than a year to live. Well after a few chemo therepies, MAJOR dietary changes and lots of exercise..its now seven years later and the cancer is in remission and my mom is reletively healthy. I guess what im saying is keep the faith, doctors dont always get it right!<P>Kerm<BR>86 GT<BR>86 2M4||||reg||14
